2026/Jun/17 06:16:40.825925 USER TC_26_6_8_4.ttcn3:63 --- LIMIT-1: Frequency Hopping (FH) not supported ---
2026/Jun/17 06:16:40.825930 USER TC_26_6_8_4.ttcn3:64 *** The spec's IdleUpdated preamble at line [1] uses     ***
2026/Jun/17 06:16:40.825935 USER TC_26_6_8_4.ttcn3:65 *** C_Test_fh (frequency hopping cell configuration).    ***
2026/Jun/17 06:16:40.825940 USER TC_26_6_8_4.ttcn3:66 *** osmo-virtphy (l1ctl_sap.c) contains:                 ***
2026/Jun/17 06:16:40.825944 USER TC_26_6_8_4.ttcn3:67 ***   OSMO_ASSERT(est_req->h == 0) /* no hopping */       ***
2026/Jun/17 06:16:40.825950 USER TC_26_6_8_4.ttcn3:68 *** Any channel activation with h=1 (hopping) crashes    ***
2026/Jun/17 06:16:40.825955 USER TC_26_6_8_4.ttcn3:69 *** the virtual PHY process immediately. This blocks     ***
2026/Jun/17 06:16:40.825960 USER TC_26_6_8_4.ttcn3:70 *** the test from even establishing the initial channel. ***
2026/Jun/17 06:16:40.825964 USER TC_26_6_8_4.ttcn3:72 --- LIMIT-2: Handover not supported in virtual environment ---
2026/Jun/17 06:16:40.825971 USER TC_26_6_8_4.ttcn3:73 *** Sub-purposes 3, 7 require HANDOVER COMMAND from BSC. ***
2026/Jun/17 06:16:40.825976 USER TC_26_6_8_4.ttcn3:74 *** osmo-virtphy and osmo-bts-virtual have no mechanism   ***
2026/Jun/17 06:16:40.825980 USER TC_26_6_8_4.ttcn3:75 *** for inter-cell or intra-cell handover simulation.    ***
2026/Jun/17 06:16:40.825985 USER TC_26_6_8_4.ttcn3:76 *** +ltree_HndOv0/1/2 and +handoverAcc() in the spec     ***
2026/Jun/17 06:16:40.825991 USER TC_26_6_8_4.ttcn3:77 *** require a real or simulated RF handover path between  ***
2026/Jun/17 06:16:40.825996 USER TC_26_6_8_4.ttcn3:78 "*** two BTS cells " & char(0, 0, 32, 20) & " impossible in the GSMTAP-only        ***"
2026/Jun/17 06:16:40.826007 USER TC_26_6_8_4.ttcn3:79 *** virtual test environment.                             ***
2026/Jun/17 06:16:40.826013 USER TC_26_6_8_4.ttcn3:81 --- LIMIT-3: Channel Assignment failure simulation not available ---
2026/Jun/17 06:16:40.826018 USER TC_26_6_8_4.ttcn3:82 *** Sub-purposes 2, 8 require ASSIGNMENT COMMAND +        ***
2026/Jun/17 06:16:40.826025 USER TC_26_6_8_4.ttcn3:83 *** ASSIGNMENT FAILURE signalling. The BSC (osmo-bsc)    ***
2026/Jun/17 06:16:40.826037 USER TC_26_6_8_4.ttcn3:84 *** manages channel assignment internally. Injecting an   ***
2026/Jun/17 06:16:40.826042 USER TC_26_6_8_4.ttcn3:85 *** assignment that is destined to fail (to test the MS   ***
2026/Jun/17 06:16:40.826047 USER TC_26_6_8_4.ttcn3:86 *** fallback to old channel + old cipher mode) requires   ***
2026/Jun/17 06:16:40.826053 USER TC_26_6_8_4.ttcn3:87 *** BSC-level control that is not exposed via the MSC     ***
2026/Jun/17 06:16:40.826058 USER TC_26_6_8_4.ttcn3:88 *** stub interface. The bsc-stub does not implement       ***
2026/Jun/17 06:16:40.826063 USER TC_26_6_8_4.ttcn3:89 *** ASSIGNMENT COMMAND injection.                         ***
